Hi Michael,

v2 is rebased on current top-of-tree (04e4201).  The only conflict was
the ChangeLog context; the board, the runner and the UART file are
unchanged from v1.

On "make check": that error means runtest can't find the board file.
baseboards/microblaze-qemu.exp only exists in a DejaGnu tree with the
patch applied, and make check is using your installed DejaGnu.  Either
point runtest at the patched tree:

  echo 'lappend boards_dir "/path/to/dejagnu/baseboards"' > ~/mb-site.exp
  export DEJAGNU=~/mb-site.exp

or install the patched DejaGnu and put its runtest first on PATH.

But I should have said this in the first mail: the board is for the GCC
testsuite, and it does nothing for binutils.  I've now run binutils
master's make check with and without it, and every result is the same
in gas, binutils and ld.  gas never runs target code.  ld does have run
tests, but it decides whether it can execute anything by running a test
program, and it reads the result from the program's exit status.  QEMU
can't hand that back.  The board reads it instead from a line printed
by DejaGnu's testglue.c, which GCC's testsuite links in and ld's
doesn't.  So ld's check fails and its run tests come out UNSUPPORTED.
For binutils, the gdb simulator (--enable-sim, microblaze-elf-run) is
the better route.

For GCC, from a combined gcc/newlib/libgloss build:

  export MB_QEMU=/path/to/qemu-system-microblaze
  export PATH=/path/to/dejagnu/contrib:$PATH     # microblaze-qemu-run
  export MB_LIBXIL=/dir/with/libxil.a
  export MB_NO_RELAX=-Wl,--no-relax              # until the __wrap_ relax fix lands
  make check-gcc RUNTESTFLAGS="--target_board=microblaze-qemu execute.exp=pr50865.c"

libxil.a is built from microblaze-qemu-libxil.c in the patched tree:

  microblaze-elf-gcc -O2 -ffreestanding -c microblaze-qemu-libxil.c -o libxil.o
  microblaze-elf-ar rc libxil.a libxil.o

Sam

